frv: FDPIC dynamic relocations are REL, say so in the dynamic tags

Since binutils 2.35 (3084d7a27b8, "ELF: Add _bfd_elf_add_dynamic_tags")
elf32_frvfdpic_size_dynamic_sections leaves the dynamic tags to the
generic code, which picks DT_RELA/DT_RELASZ/DT_RELAENT and DT_PLTREL =
DT_RELA from elf_backend_rela_plts_and_copies_p.  That defaults to
elf_backend_default_use_rela_p, which FDPIC sets to 1, while the dynamic
relocations it writes are REL (.rel.dyn, .rel.plt).  Before, the backend
added DT_REL, DT_RELSZ, DT_RELENT and DT_PLTREL = DT_REL itself.

The result: ld-uClibc.so has "RELA 0x0, RELASZ 0" next to a .rel.dyn
with 58 entries, so the loader never relocates itself, and libc.so and
every program say PLTREL = RELA.  Nothing dynamically linked runs.

--- a/bfd/elf32-frv.c	2026-10-26 09:53:05.984135024 +0100
+++ b/bfd/elf32-frv.c	2026-10-26 09:53:06.264141914 +0100
@@ -6867,6 +6867,10 @@
 /* We use REL for dynamic relocations only.  */
 #undef elf_backend_default_use_rela_p
 #define elf_backend_default_use_rela_p	1
+/* ... so DT_PLTREL, DT_REL, DT_RELSZ and DT_RELENT describe them, not
+   the RELA tags _bfd_elf_add_dynamic_tags derives from the above.  */
+#undef elf_backend_rela_plts_and_copies_p
+#define elf_backend_rela_plts_and_copies_p	0
 
 #undef elf_backend_omit_section_dynsym
 #define elf_backend_omit_section_dynsym _frvfdpic_link_omit_section_dynsym
